und the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{5-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319349 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {4}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319350 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{5}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319351 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{3}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319352 :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$” is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$” is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$” is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$” only."] [17592186319362 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319363 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}3{sec}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319364 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319366 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319367 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319369 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{40}{64-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$artanh\\,(${{field-2}}$)$"] [17592186319370 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319371 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319372 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\sqrt[3]{{s}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319373 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{\\sqrt[5]{{t}^{13}}}\\,\\text{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319386 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186319387 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }